             & = (a^3 + b^3) + 3ab(a + b)
   \end{align*}

6. We know that $a+b=5$ from the problem statement, so we can substitute this into our equation:
   \begin{align*}
   (a + b)^3 & = (a^3 + b^3) + 3ab(5) \\
             & = (a^3 + b^3) + 15ab
   \end{align*}

7. Now we need to find $(a+b)^3$. We can do this by cubing $a+b=5$:
   \begin{align*}
   (a + b)^3 & = 5^3 \\
