To solve this problem, we need to find the value of $f(g(-2))$. We can start by substituting $-2$ into the function $g(x)$.

\begin{align*}
g(-2) &= (x - 1)^2\\
&= (-2 - 1)^2\\
&= (-3)^2\\
&= 9
\end{align*}

Now that we have found $g(-2)$, we can substitute this value into the function $f(x)$.

\begin{align*}
f(g(-2)) &= f(9)\\
&= 3 \cdot 9 + 2\\
&= 27 + 2\\
&= \boxed{29}
\end{align*}

Therefore, $f(g(-2)) = 29$.

